{"book":19,"chapter":87,"context":{"chapter":87,"title":"Born in Zion","summary":"God loves Zion, and he enrolls even Egyptians, Babylonians, Philistines, Tyrians and Cushites as citizens 'born there.' All the springs of joy are in her.","background":"Title: 'A Psalm or Song for the sons of Korah.' A short song of Zion with a remarkable vision of former enemies counted as native-born. 'Rahab' here is a poetic name for Egypt (compare Isaiah 51:9). Paul speaks of 'Jerusalem which is above... the mother of us all' (Galatians 4:26).","customs":[{"term":"The city register","verses":"87:6","note":"Cities kept lists of citizens by family; being enrolled meant belonging (Isaiah 4:3; Ezra 2:62)."}],"watchFor":["'Glorious things are spoken of thee, O city of God' (v. 3).","'This man was born there' repeats three times (vv. 4–6)."],"connections":["Isaiah 2:2-3","Isaiah 19:24-25","Isaiah 51:9","Galatians 4:26"]},"verses":{"0":{"w":[["לִבְנֵי","livnei-","H1121","HR/Ncmpc","of [the] sons of"],["קֹרַח","korach","H7141","HNpm","Korah"],["מִזְמוֹר","mizmor","H4210","HNcmsa","a psalm"],["שִׁיר","shir","H7892","HNcmsa","a song"]]},"1":{"w":[["יְסוּדָתוֹ","yesudato","H3248","HNcfsc/Sp3ms","foundation his"],["בְּהַרְרֵי","beharei-","H2042","HR/Ncmpc","[is] among [the] mountains of"],["קֹדֶשׁ","kodesh","H6944","HNcmsa","holiness"]],"x":[[23028016,23028016,13],[23056007,23056007,12],[23002002,23002003,9],[49002020,49002022,9],[40016018,40016018,8],[19048001,19048002,7],[38008003,38008003,7],[46003010,46003011,7],[19068016,19068016,6],[14003001,14003001,5]],"xn":13},"2":{"w":[["אֹהֵב","'ohev","H157","HVqrmsa","[is] loving"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["שַׁעֲרֵי","sha'arei","H8179","HNcmpc","[the] gates of"],["צִיּוֹן","tziyon","H6726","HNpl","Zion"],["מִכֹּל","mikol","H3605","HR/Ncmsc","more than all"],["מִשְׁכְּנוֹת","mishkenot","H4908","HNcfpc","[the] dwelling places of"],["יַעֲקֹב","ya'ako","H3290","HNpm","Jacob"]],"x":[[5012005,5012005,7],[19132013,19132014,7],[1907806